# SafePay JSON request examples.
# Replace the email and IDs with records from your simulated database.
# In Postman, select Body > raw > JSON and copy the corresponding JSON object.
# The source account must cover pending PROTECTED/HARD_HOLD amounts plus INR 5,000.
# Reuse an initiation's Idempotency-Key only when retrying that same request.
# Reuse a cancellation's Idempotency-Key when retrying that cancellation too.
# Restart the backend after these changes: Hibernate ddl-auto=update adds the
# cancellation-key and authorized/released timestamp columns to existing tables.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@userEmail = demo@example.com
@accountId = 1000001
@beneficiaryId = 1
@transactionId = 42

### Optional simulator setup: use an account without existing pending payments.
# After this, the INR 75,000 payment below has a 60-second protection window.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{accountId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "balance": 90000.00
}

### Add a beneficiary: account and user details are in the body.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/beneficiaries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountId": {{accountId}},
  "userEmail": "{{userEmail}}",
  "beneficiaryName": "Demo Payee",
  "bankAccountNumber": "123456789012",
  "ifsc": "SBIN0001234"
}

### Initiate a payment: purpose is optional. Use the returned transactionId below.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/transactions/initiate
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: initiate-demo-001

{
  "fromAccountId": {{accountId}},
  "beneficiaryId": {{beneficiaryId}},
  "amount": 75000.00,
  "purpose": "Demo transfer",
  "userEmail": "{{userEmail}}"
}

### While the INR 75,000 payment is protected, this must return HTTP 400.
# With a balance of INR 90,000, only INR 10,000 is spendable after the hold/minimum.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/transactions/initiate
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: reservation-check-002

{
  "fromAccountId": {{accountId}},
  "beneficiaryId": {{beneficiaryId}},
  "amount": 10001.00,
  "purpose": "Pending funds check",
  "userEmail": "{{userEmail}}"
}

### Cancel a payment during its protection window.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/transactions/{{transactionId}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: cancel-demo-001

{
  "userEmail": "{{userEmail}}"
}

### Change beneficiary status: use ACTIVE or INACTIVE.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/beneficiaries/{{beneficiaryId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "INACTIVE",
  "userEmail": "{{userEmail}}"
}

# Existing read-only GET endpoints still use query parameters and have no body:
# GET /api/transactions/{transactionId}?userEmail=demo@example.com
# GET /api/transactions?userEmail=demo@example.com&state=PROTECTED
# GET /api/beneficiaries?userEmail=demo@example.com

# Additional manual checks (use a fresh initiation key for each new scenario):
# - Repeat an initiation with the same key/body: same transactionId, no extra debit.
# - Change its amount but reuse its key: HTTP 409.
# - Cancel before expiry: response state CANCELLED with cancelledAt populated.
# - Repeat that cancellation using the same key: same result, no duplicate audit.
# - Cancel after expiry, or cancel a settled payment: HTTP 400.
# - Allow a fresh HIGH payment to expire: polling reports SETTLED after the job runs.
# - Submit 10000.001 as an amount: HTTP 400, no rounded/incorrect risk decision.
# - History/detail responses now include amount, beneficiary details and timestamps.
